  "title": "Check Payments",
  "summary": "At a first glance, it feels like in 2026 check payments should be obsolete, but they still aren't. One study found that nearly 80-83% of firms with revenue under $10 million use checks for business payments. In the nonprofit space this is sometimes even higher. Even the largest national DAFs struggle to push their ACH rates above 50%. There are a few reasons why nonprofits/grantmakers still use checks which was written about here.",
